      "category": "other",
      "components": ["H4"],
      "pins": ["H4.1", "H4.2", "H4.3", "H4.4", "H4.1", "H4.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "I2C_SDA", "I2C_SCL", "GND", "+24V"],
      "observed": "Reference designator H4 is used twice: once for the 4-pin PB_1.25mm LiDAR header in the Water Height Sensor block and once for the 2-pin MC_0.2\" ATO valve connector in the Main Pump & Valve Drivers block.",
      "expected": "Reference designators must be unique. The specification assigns H4 to the ATO valve MC_0.2\" connector; the LiDAR header is not part of the intended wired design.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "r2 has `H2` as a single `MSTBA_0.2\"` and `H3`/`H4` as `MC_0.2\"` pairs"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Water Height Sensor block: H4 PB_1.25mm; ATO Valve block: H4 MC_0.2\"."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Creates BOM/assembly ambiguity: one connector may be omitted or placed with the wrong footprint, potentially losing either the ATO valve connection or the unintended LiDAR header.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains a wired PR1 LiDAR header on the main I2C bus even though the specification says PR1 must be unwired, and the added PB_1.25mm header reuses reference designator H4 already assigned to the ATO valve connector."
}

